#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Concern: the mechanical gates a change clears, here and replayed in CI — annotations, then comment budget | Non-concern: the semantic review, attested in the commit message | IO: (tree) -> pass/fail
# Enable per clone: git config core.hooksPath .githooks   Bypass: git commit --no-verify
set -euo pipefail

if [ -x target/release/annotated-tree ]; then
	run=(target/release/annotated-tree)
elif [ -x target/debug/annotated-tree ]; then
	run=(target/debug/annotated-tree)
else
	run=(cargo run --quiet --)
fi

# Flagless: .annotated-tree.toml carries the gate, and CI replays this script.
"${run[@]}" --strict-check . || {
	echo "" >&2
	echo "pre-commit: ANNOTATION GATE FAILED (see above)" >&2
	exit 1
}

# Pinned to a rev and cached under target/, so a fresh clone gates without a manual install step.
REV=db39b2eeeefbe31a64030577206737caadc4f2ac
LINT=target/lint-tools/comment-crusher/$REV/bin/comment-crusher

[ -x "$LINT" ] || cargo install --git https://github.com/fredrikolis/comment-crusher --rev "$REV" --root "target/lint-tools/comment-crusher/$REV" --quiet comment-crusher >&2

"$LINT" . --format editor 1>&2 || {
	echo "" >&2
	echo "pre-commit: COMMENT GATE FAILED — what this gate does and does not measure:" >&2
	cat >&2 <<'STANDARD'
It measures size, never quality: a comment ratio per file, the length of any one comment block,
and the length of a prose document. It cannot tell a good comment from a bad one and does not try.

Tripping it is NOT an instruction to delete comments until the number passes. It asks why this
function needed a block of explanation, or why this document grew so long; the usual answer is
that the code is wrong, not the comment. Fix the shape: extract it, rename it, split it.

Never widen a bound in .comment-crusher.toml to make a file pass. The bound is the detector, and a
bigger number only hides what it found. The one honest exception is a file whose comments are not
commentary at all — clap doc comments that compile into --help — and it states that as its reason.

The bar a comment must clear to earn its space: git-agent-verdict --standards programming
STANDARD
	exit 1
}
